{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "1CH",
  "chapter": 11,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then all Israel gathered themselves to David to Hebron, saying, Behold, we ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy bone and thy flesh.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And moreover in time past, even when Saul was king, thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "wast",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he that leddest out and broughtest in Israel: and the LORD thy God said to thee, Thou shalt feed my people Israel, and thou shalt be ruler over my people Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore came all the elders of Israel to the king to Hebron; and David made a covenant with them in Hebron before the LORD; and they anointed David king over Israel, according to the word of the LORD by Samuel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David and all Israel went to Jerusalem, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Jebus; where the Jebusites ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", the inhabitants of the land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the inhabitants of Jebus said to David, Thou shalt not come hither. Nevertheless David took the castle of Zion, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the city of David.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David said, Whoever smiteth the Jebusites first shall be chief and captain. So Joab the son of Zeruiah went up first, and was chief.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David dwelt in the castle; therefore they called it, The city of David.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he built the city around, even from Millo around: and Joab repaired the rest of the city.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So David became greater and greater: for the LORD of hosts ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the chief of the mighty men whom David had, who strengthened themselves with him in his kingdom, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with all Israel, to make him king according to the word of the LORD concerning Israel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the number of the mighty men whom David had; Jashobeam a Hachmonite, the chief of the captains: he lifted his spear against three hundred slain ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "by him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at one time.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And after him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Eleazar the son of Dodo, the Ahohite, who ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the three mighties.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He was with David at Pas-dammim, and there the Philistines were gathered to battle, where was a parcel of ground full of barley; and the people fled from before the Philistines.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And they set themselves in the midst of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " parcel, and delivered it, and slew the Philistines; and the LORD saved ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by a great deliverance.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now three of the thirty captains went down to the rock to David, into the cave of Adullam; and the host of the Philistines encamped in the valley of Rephaim.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " then in the hold, and the Philistines' garrison ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " then at Beth-lehem.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And David longed, and said, Oh that one would give me drink of the water of the well of Beth-lehem, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at the gate!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the three broke through the host of the Philistines, and drew water out of the well of Beth-lehem, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by the gate, and took ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and brought ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to David: but David would not drink ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it, but poured it out to the LORD,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said, My God forbid it me, that I should do this thing: shall I drink the blood of these men that have put their lives in jeopardy? for with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the jeopardy of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " their lives they brought it. Therefore he would not drink it. These things did these three mightiest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Abishai the brother of Joab, he was chief of the three: for lifting his spear against three hundred, he slew ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and had a name among the three.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Of the three, he was more honorable than the two; for he was their captain: but he attained not to the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "first",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " three.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, the son of a valiant man of Kabzeel, who had done many acts; he slew two lion-like men of Moab: also he went down and slew a lion in a pit in a snowy day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he slew an Egyptian, a man of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "great",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " stature, five cubits high; and in the Egyptian's hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a spear like a weaver's beam; and he went down to him with a staff, and plucked the spear out of the Egyptian's hand, and slew him with his own spear.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " did Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and had the name among the three mighties.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he was honorable among the thirty, but attained not to the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "first",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " three: and David set him over his guard.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also the valiant men of the armies ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", Asahel the brother of Joab, Elhanan the son of Dodo of Beth-lehem,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Shammoth the Harorite, Helez the Pelonite,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ira the son of Ikkesh the Tekoite, Abiezer the Antothite,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sibbecai the Hushathite, Ilai the Ahohite,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Maharai the Netophathite, Heled the son of Baanah the Netophathite,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ithai the son of Ribai of Gibeah, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that pertained",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the children of Benjamin, Benaiah the Pirathonite,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1CH.11.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:1CH.11.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hurai of the brooks of Gaash, Abiel the Arbathite,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
